            <ArticleTitle>FcRn is mother's milk to allergen tolerance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1084/jem.20172022</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this issue Ohsaki et al. (https://doi.org/10.1084/jem.20171163) explain how breastfeeding can prevent the onset of food allergies in offspring by instructing T reg formation via neonatal Fc receptor (FcRn)-mediated transfer and uptake of allergen-containing IgG immune complexes (Ig-ICs) by gut dendritic cells (DCs).</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2018 Lambrecht.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
